
====================================================================================================
RouteFollower on the JVM — what it commands, and what reaches the motors
====================================================================================================
RouteFollower.kt, MotorSettings.kt and DriveArbiter.kt are the real classes under app/src/main.
The transmit loop is called as the app calls it (MainActivity.kt:604-609):
    DriveArbiter.resolve(
        route = if (following) routeSpeeds else null,
        manual = motorSettings.speedsFor(command),
        avoidance = if (avoidanceActive) avoidanceDecision else null,
    ).frame()
and the autonomous loop's per-branch routeSpeeds from MainActivity.kt:694-750.
TICK: one FOLLOW_TICK_MS = 100 ms pass of MainActivity.kt:665-757.


====================================================================================================
CASE 0 — arbitration: what reaches the motors while a route is following
====================================================================================================
  the autonomous loop stores the follower's own pair into routeSpeeds:
  Drive(180,128)           follower frame=c180,128       routeSpeeds=c180,128       transmitted=c180,128
  Pivot(-154,143)          follower frame=c-154,143      routeSpeeds=c-154,143      transmitted=c-154,143
  Hold(bad fix)            follower frame=c0,0           routeSpeeds=c0,0           transmitted=c0,0
  Arrived                  follower frame=c0,0           routeSpeeds=c0,0           transmitted=c0,0
  CHECK PASS: a clear path sends the follower's own pair, not the controller's cruise
  CHECK PASS: the controller's corridor steering is laid on the follower's pair
  CHECK PASS: a drop or a blocked path stops the car even with a route loaded
  CHECK PASS: a depth feed that went quiet stops the car too - it is not a clear road
  CHECK PASS: with nobody driving and depth live, the controller drives itself (the AUTO switch)
  CHECK PASS: with avoidance off, the route or the manual command goes out

