====================================================================================================
CASE (d) — stalled track: no progress for > 15 s (stuckSeconds = 15)
====================================================================================================
  'sent' below is the transmit loop with avoidanceActive=true and depth unavailable: the
  controller reports STOP: DEPTH UNAVAILABLE, which stops the car, so nothing moves until
  the depth feed is back (the walker is told, by MainActivity's no-sensing warning):
  t=  0.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t=  2.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t=  4.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t=  6.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t=  8.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t= 10.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t= 12.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t= 14.0s Drive(left=180, right=128)                     sent=c0,0
  t= 15.1s Hold(not making progress toward "Head north 9 m") sent=c0,0
  first Hold at tick 151 = 15.1 s
  CHECK PASS: the stuck detector fires after stuckSeconds (15 s), not before

